---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { href } from "../../lib/url.js";
// The full policy's last-changed date, from the same generated twin /privacy/policy/ renders (#5920).
import policy from "../../privacy/policy.json";
---

<Base title="Privacy" top={null} description="What is published here, what never is, and how a private record becomes public content.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:760px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px">
      <p class="label">Privacy</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:40px">Only deliberately published figures appear here.</h1>
      <p class="dek" style="font-size:19px">
        Selected health measurements are published, some blood-test results and a biological-age estimate among them. Journals, progress photos,
        genetic findings, his actual age and other sensitive records stay private. A private record reaches a public page only through the
        platform's publication boundary and, where a person's words or a picture are concerned, an explicit approval. Readers' entries are never
        collected on these pages.
      </p>
      <p>
        The full policy — what a subscriber's address is used for and how to leave, cookies and tracking, your rights, the AI disclaimer and the
        permanence contract — is <a href={href("/privacy/policy/")}>the current privacy policy</a>, last changed on {policy.updated}. The policy
        as it stood at the site's relaunch on 1 November 2026 is kept as <a href="/reference/2026-11-01-privacy-v5/">an archived copy</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:14px">
        This site stores the date of your last visit in your browser — the date of the front page's edition you last saw — to show what has
        changed since then. The date is not sent to the site or used for advertising or analytics. Some older pages still served from the site's
        earlier design keep other small settings in your browser; the full policy's section on cookies and tracking says what they are.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
